WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.779
Improving Soft Skills:

2
00:00:02.059 --> 00:00:03.297
The 90-Day Plan.

3
00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:07.481
Day 93 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

4
00:00:09.231 --> 00:00:10.255
The key idea.

5
00:00:10.535 --> 00:00:12.348
What gets measured gets improved.

6
00:00:12.628 --> 00:00:16.489
Score yourself, pick your track, and spend 10 to 20 minutes a day on it.

7
00:00:17.839 --> 00:00:18.693
Part 1.

8
00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:19.890
Step 1:

9
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.301
Self-assessment.

10
00:00:22.551 --> 00:00:25.431
Score each from 1 (rarely) to 5 (always).

11
00:00:25.711 --> 00:00:27.481
Redo it every 30 days.

12
00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:30.197
Here is a quick table:

13
00:00:30.477 --> 00:00:31.607
Skill, and Score.

14
00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:32.527
1.

15
00:00:32.807 --> 00:00:33.511
Skill:

16
00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:36.181
I state my main point in the first sentence.

17
00:00:36.461 --> 00:00:37.165
2.

18
00:00:37.445 --> 00:00:38.149
Skill:

19
00:00:38.429 --> 00:00:40.775
I speak up in meetings without being asked.

20
00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:41.802
3.

21
00:00:42.082 --> 00:00:42.786
Skill:

22
00:00:43.066 --> 00:00:46.799
I can explain a technical issue to a non-technical person.

23
00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:47.783
4.

24
00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:48.767
Skill:

25
00:00:49.047 --> 00:00:51.927
I raise risks early, before they become problems.

26
00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:52.975
5.

27
00:00:53.255 --> 00:00:53.959
Skill:

28
00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:56.821
I say no or push back politely when needed.

29
00:00:57.101 --> 00:00:57.847
6.

30
00:00:58.127 --> 00:00:58.831
Skill:

31
00:00:59.111 --> 00:01:01.309
I give feedback that's specific and kind.

32
00:01:01.589 --> 00:01:02.335
7.

33
00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:03.319
Skill:

34
00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:05.370
I listen without interrupting.

35
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.333
8.

36
00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:07.317
Skill:

37
00:01:07.597 --> 00:01:10.775
I stay calm when someone is upset or criticises me.

38
00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:12.872
9.

39
00:01:13.152 --> 00:01:13.856
Skill:

40
00:01:14.136 --> 00:01:17.379
I can make small talk with a stranger for 3 plus minutes.

41
00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:18.363
10.

42
00:01:18.643 --> 00:01:19.347
Skill:

43
00:01:19.627 --> 00:01:22.187
I write clear, short messages and emails.

44
00:01:23.537 --> 00:01:24.795
10 to 25:

45
00:01:25.075 --> 00:01:27.230
Beginner track, 26 to 40:

46
00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.771
Intermediate track, 41 to 50:

47
00:01:30.051 --> 00:01:31.161
Advanced track.

48
00:01:32.511 --> 00:01:33.385
Part 2.

49
00:01:33.665 --> 00:01:34.583
Step 2:

50
00:01:34.863 --> 00:01:35.887
Choose your track.

51
00:01:37.137 --> 00:01:38.118
Beginner track.

52
00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.273
Month 1:

53
00:01:39.553 --> 00:01:40.555
Foundations.

54
00:01:40.835 --> 00:01:44.099
Read Communication Principles and Building Confidence.

55
00:01:44.379 --> 00:01:46.321
Speak at least once in every meeting.

56
00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.691
Use the stand-up format every day.

57
00:01:48.971 --> 00:01:51.574
One 10-minute Master Prompt role-play a day.

58
00:01:51.854 --> 00:01:54.542
Learn 5 phrases a week from the Phrase Bank.

59
00:01:54.822 --> 00:01:55.739
Month 2:

60
00:01:56.019 --> 00:01:56.937
Workplace.

61
00:01:58.287 --> 00:02:01.465
Prepare an agenda for every one-on-one with your manager.

62
00:02:01.745 --> 00:02:03.836
Write one bug report using SBAR.

63
00:02:04.116 --> 00:02:07.188
Ask one clarifying question on every new task.

64
00:02:07.468 --> 00:02:11.500
Have a 5-minute conversation with someone outside your team each week.

65
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.697
Month 3:

66
00:02:12.977 --> 00:02:13.916
Visibility.

67
00:02:14.196 --> 00:02:16.436
Give a 5-minute demo or knowledge-share.

68
00:02:16.716 --> 00:02:20.343
Practise one Everyday Life scenario in real life each week.

69
00:02:21.693 --> 00:02:22.823
Ask your manager:

70
00:02:23.103 --> 00:02:26.218
What's one thing about how I communicate that I could improve?

71
00:02:27.568 --> 00:02:28.784
Intermediate track.

72
00:02:29.064 --> 00:02:29.939
Month 1:

73
00:02:30.219 --> 00:02:31.157
Influence.

74
00:02:31.437 --> 00:02:33.528
Use PREP in every design discussion.

75
00:02:33.808 --> 00:02:37.776
Push back on one unrealistic estimate using options, not no.

76
00:02:38.056 --> 00:02:41.235
Mentor one junior with a weekly 30-minute session.

77
00:02:41.515 --> 00:02:42.432
Month 2:

78
00:02:42.712 --> 00:02:44.099
Up-level your audience.

79
00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:48.091
Write a one-page decision doc for a non-technical stakeholder.

80
00:02:48.371 --> 00:02:50.888
Present at a team-wide or cross-team meeting.

81
00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:56.057
Practise the CEO 30-second update with AI 5 times.

82
00:02:56.337 --> 00:02:57.254
Month 3:

83
00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:58.878
Hard conversations.

84
00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:02.145
Have one difficult conversation you've been avoiding.

85
00:03:02.425 --> 00:03:04.046
Run a blameless post-mortem.

86
00:03:04.326 --> 00:03:08.913
Get 360 degrees feedback from a peer, a junior and your manager.

87
00:03:10.263 --> 00:03:12.673
Advanced track (8 to 15 plus yrs).

88
00:03:12.953 --> 00:03:13.828
Month 1:

89
00:03:14.108 --> 00:03:15.409
Executive presence.

90
00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:19.380
Shorten every update by 30%; lead with the decision.

91
00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:24.033
Pre-wire important meetings (talk to key people one-on-one beforehand).

92
00:03:24.313 --> 00:03:28.836
Turn one technical proposal into a business case (cost, risk, revenue).

93
00:03:29.116 --> 00:03:30.033
Month 2:

94
00:03:30.313 --> 00:03:31.551
Multiply others.

95
00:03:31.831 --> 00:03:34.967
Coach two people on communication, using this playbook.

96
00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:39.300
Delegate one high-visibility task and sponsor the person publicly.

97
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.191
Facilitate (don't dominate) a design review: speak last.

98
00:03:44.471 --> 00:03:45.389
Month 3:

99
00:03:45.669 --> 00:03:46.799
External voice.

100
00:03:47.079 --> 00:03:50.045
Give a talk at a meetup or internal tech conference.

101
00:03:50.325 --> 00:03:52.693
Write a blog post or internal article.

102
00:03:52.973 --> 00:03:55.277
Practise the networking scripts at one event.

103
00:03:56.627 --> 00:03:57.523
Part 3.

104
00:03:57.803 --> 00:03:58.720
Step 3:

105
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.493
Daily 10-minute drills.

106
00:04:01.743 --> 00:04:03.109
Here is a quick table:

107
00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:04.989
Drill, and How, and Builds.

108
00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:06.954
The 60-second explain.

109
00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:07.895
How:

110
00:04:08.175 --> 00:04:10.586
Pick a concept (Kafka, caching, OAuth).

111
00:04:10.866 --> 00:04:14.685
Explain it aloud in 60 s to an imaginary 12-year-old.

112
00:04:14.965 --> 00:04:15.754
Builds:

113
00:04:16.034 --> 00:04:16.866
Clarity.

114
00:04:17.146 --> 00:04:18.426
Rewrite one message.

115
00:04:18.706 --> 00:04:19.367
How:

116
00:04:19.647 --> 00:04:21.333
Take a Slack message you sent.

117
00:04:21.613 --> 00:04:24.087
Make it 30% shorter with the point first.

118
00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:25.157
Builds:

119
00:04:25.437 --> 00:04:26.269
Brevity.

120
00:04:26.549 --> 00:04:27.445
Shadowing.

121
00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:28.386
How:

122
00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:32.527
Play a 1-minute clip of a good speaker (TED, a podcast).

123
00:04:32.807 --> 00:04:35.005
Repeat each sentence right after them.

124
00:04:35.285 --> 00:04:36.074
Builds:

125
00:04:36.354 --> 00:04:37.527
Fluency, pace.

126
00:04:37.807 --> 00:04:39.023
Record and review.

127
00:04:39.303 --> 00:04:39.965
How:

128
00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:42.207
Record a mock stand-up on your phone.

129
00:04:42.487 --> 00:04:43.981
Watch it once at 1x.

130
00:04:44.261 --> 00:04:45.050
Builds:

131
00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.439
Voice, fillers.

132
00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.914
AI role-play.

133
00:04:48.194 --> 00:04:48.855
How:

134
00:04:49.135 --> 00:04:52.037
Run the Master Prompt on today's real situation.

135
00:04:52.317 --> 00:04:53.106
Builds:

136
00:04:53.386 --> 00:04:54.239
Everything.

137
00:04:54.519 --> 00:04:55.543
Word of the day.

138
00:04:55.823 --> 00:04:56.485
How:

139
00:04:56.765 --> 00:05:00.541
Learn one professional phrase and use it in a real conversation.

140
00:05:00.821 --> 00:05:01.610
Builds:

141
00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:02.957
Vocabulary.

142
00:05:04.307 --> 00:05:05.523
Reflection journal.

143
00:05:05.803 --> 00:05:06.464
How:

144
00:05:06.744 --> 00:05:07.704
3 lines:

145
00:05:07.984 --> 00:05:10.544
What I said, How it landed, What I'll try next.

146
00:05:10.824 --> 00:05:11.613
Builds:

147
00:05:11.893 --> 00:05:12.960
Self-awareness.

148
00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.227
Part 4.

149
00:05:15.507 --> 00:05:16.467
Step 4:

150
00:05:16.747 --> 00:05:17.793
Measure progress.

151
00:05:19.043 --> 00:05:21.603
Redo the self-assessment every 30 days.

152
00:05:21.883 --> 00:05:24.464
Count: how many times did you speak up this week?

153
00:05:24.744 --> 00:05:27.539
How many messages did you rewrite before sending?

154
00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:29.525
Ask for feedback each quarter:

155
00:05:29.805 --> 00:05:32.728
On a scale of 1 to 10, how clear are my updates?

156
00:05:33.008 --> 00:05:34.352
What would make them a 10?

157
00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.662
Part 5.

158
00:05:36.942 --> 00:05:38.329
Practice conversation:

159
00:05:38.609 --> 00:05:40.998
Asking for feedback on your communication.

160
00:05:42.248 --> 00:05:44.275
Here is how the conversation goes.

161
00:05:44.555 --> 00:05:46.603
Could I ask for some feedback?

162
00:05:46.883 --> 00:05:49.549
I'm working on my communication this quarter.

163
00:05:49.829 --> 00:05:50.747
Of course.

164
00:05:51.027 --> 00:05:55.251
On a scale of 1 to 10, how clear are my updates in stand-ups?

165
00:05:55.531 --> 00:05:56.704
Maybe a 6.

166
00:05:56.984 --> 00:05:59.352
They're accurate, but sometimes too detailed.

167
00:05:59.632 --> 00:06:00.763
That's helpful.

168
00:06:01.043 --> 00:06:02.643
What would make them a 9?

169
00:06:03.993 --> 00:06:05.593
The conversation continues.

170
00:06:05.873 --> 00:06:09.009
Start with the result, then only the important detail.

171
00:06:09.289 --> 00:06:10.739
Keep it under a minute.

172
00:06:11.019 --> 00:06:11.958
Okay.

173
00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.478
I'll try that for the next two weeks.

174
00:06:14.758 --> 00:06:16.998
Could we check again at the end of the month?

175
00:06:17.278 --> 00:06:18.601
Sure, let's do that.

176
00:06:19.951 --> 00:06:21.487
That's the end of this lesson.

177
00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:26.439
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

178
00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:32.820
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

